.PP
.B run_manual_sync
returns with
.B pending
set to true after the configured commands start in the background.  Poll
.B app_state.state.sync_in_progress
until it becomes false before checking the command result or refreshed mail
state.  The flag remains true until the post-sync search refresh also finishes.
Non-fixture harness checks may pass
.B test_refresh_delay_ms
(maximum 5000) to keep that refresh pending while testing responsiveness and
cancellation behavior.  Normal UI and command-palette syncs do not add this
delay.
.PP
.B compose_send
normally returns with
.B pending
set to true after the composed snapshot is queued.  Poll
.B app_state.state.send_in_progress
until it becomes false before checking
.BR last_send_report ,
.BR last_error ,
or send-related file changes.  If sending would permanently remove an active
saved draft,
.B compose_send
instead reports
.B pending_confirmation
and waits for the typed
.B send_composer
dialog.  Unsaved sends still start directly.  Accepted cleanup retains the
existing draft-identity and composer-generation checks.  If the primary window
closes while a send is pending, the application remains alive until send
finalization completes.
.PP
.B close_main_window
closes only the primary window after returning its response, unless dirty
compose state first defers the close behind a confirmation.  Standalone message
windows are left open.
.PP
In fixture mode,
.B draft_list_state
reports whether the rendered Saved drafts section, explicit empty state,
bounded scroller, rows, and per-selection Delete button are mapped.  It also
reports the selected row, compose fields, active draft, and fixture persistence
paths.
.B activate_draft_by_index
selects a row and emits the real list activation signal.
.B click_delete_selected_draft
emits the real Delete button click and reports whether the selected draft file
was removed.  These three UI-test controls are rejected outside fixture mode;
the older select, load, and delete commands remain compatibility controls.
Load and delete still use the same confirmation policy as their rendered UI
routes.
.SS Confirmation dialog seam
Destructive actions and actions that replace the composer can defer instead of
running immediately.  This includes draft discard and permanent deletion,
dirty composer replacement by New, reply, forward, or draft-load actions, and
other routes such as window close.  A command that
starts this flow reports
.B pending_confirmation
set to true where applicable.  The
.B pending_confirmation
command is the authoritative state check.
.PP
Sending an active saved draft is a typed
.B send_composer
confirmation because accepted transport cleanup permanently deletes that
draft.  Unsaved sends do not add this confirmation.
.PP
.B pending_confirmation
reports either a null
.B pending
value or the captured action's identifier, typed kind, dialog title,
confirmation-button label, and current GTK visibility.  It also reports
.B last_completion
and the current compose fields, active draft, recovery and named-draft paths,
visible status, and last operation or error.  Only one action can be pending at
a time.
.PP
Drive the real modal dialog with
.BR respond_confirmation .
Its
.B response
argument must be
.B accept
or
.BR reject ;
the optional
.B id
defaults to the current pending action and protects against responding to a
different dialog.  For example:
.PP
.nf
{"command":"respond_confirmation","args":{"id":1,"response":"reject"}}
.fi
.PP
The command emits the real GTK dialog response rather than calling the action
directly.  Reject cancels without executing the captured replacement or
destructive action.  Accept revalidates current send or sync eligibility, then
executes that captured action once.  The returned
.B last_completion
reports whether it was accepted and whether it succeeded.  While a
confirmation is pending, harness mutations are rejected without changing its
identifier, dialog, compose state, recovery bytes, or persisted draft bytes;
read-only queries remain available.
.PP
Confirmation inspection and response are normally fixture-only.  A
non-fixture harness with
.B automation.allow_live_send_test=true
may use them only while the pending action is exactly
.BR send_composer .
This narrow exception lets custom-transport tests drive the real saved-draft
Send modal without exposing other live confirmations.
.PP
.B save_selected_attachment
and its
.B save_attachment
compatibility spelling open the normal GTK save chooser when the
.B dir
argument is omitted.  In fixture mode,
.B attachment_test_state
reports the pending chooser identifier, sanitized suggested name, visibility,
private Open directory, and fake-opener calls.  A test can then send:
.PP
.nf
{"command":"respond_attachment_save","args":{"id":1,"response":"accept","path":"/full/target"}}
.fi
.PP
or use
.B "response":"cancel".
Accept uses the complete target path and creates a numbered sibling rather than
replacing an existing file.  Cancel succeeds without writing or changing the
last operation, error, or status.  These two inspection/response commands are
rejected outside fixture mode.  Supplying an explicit
.B dir
to
.B save_selected_attachment
is a synchronous storage-test bypass and does not exercise the chooser.
.PP
Attachment Open writes a safely named file below an application-owned private
temporary directory before launching it.  The directory has mode 0700 on Unix
and is removed on normal process exit.  Fixture mode records the path in a fake
opener rather than starting an external application.
.PP
After
.BR open_settings ,
the fixture-only
.B settings_test_state
command reports the real dialog identifier and visible controls, the requested
theme and live resolved
.B theme_bg_color
and luminance with raw GTK properties, the configured preview limit, and the
actual rendered preview label's line limit, visibility, and text.
.B respond_settings
drives that same GTK dialog's response signal.  It accepts optional
.BR id ,
.BR theme ,
.BR thread_preview_lines ,
and
.B show_thread_preview
arguments and a
.B response
of
.BR apply ,
.BR save ,
or
.BR close .
For example:
.PP
.nf
{"command":"respond_settings","args":{"response":"apply","theme":"dark","thread_preview_lines":3,"show_thread_preview":true}}
.fi
.PP
Invalid theme or preview values leave the dialog open and change neither
runtime state nor the config file.
.B apply
changes the running window without writing;
.B save
writes and then applies.  These two inspection/response commands are rejected
outside fixture mode.  The older
.B save_settings
command persists only its basic direct-test fields and does not exercise the
dialog.
.SH SAFETY
Keep the socket local to the user session and use a token.  Prefer fixture data
for test-harness runs.  Fixture mode does not run configured receive,
database-update, or external-send commands; sends are captured locally and tag
changes are confined to the disposable fixture database.
.PP
On a non-fixture account,
.B automation.allow_live_send_test
must be true for
.B compose_send
and
.B automation.allow_live_tag_test
must be true for tag mutations.  Both default to false, and the gates also
apply when the operation is requested through
.BR run_command .
Non-fixture sync retains its separate explicit
.B [sync]
enablement.  Draft commands can change configured local files.  Attachment Save
uses the GTK chooser, while Attachment Open uses private temporary storage;
both are intentionally outside the send/tag gates.  The explicit attachment
.B dir
bypass writes to the requested directory and should be used only when that
local change is intended.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I artifacts/screenshots/
Default screenshot output directory for test-harness screenshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notm (1),
